+# Glossary
+
+- **Account** — a member's record of money: charges and payments. Every member
+  has one from registration, with nothing in it.
+- **Active hold** — a hold that is waiting or ready. Fulfilled, cancelled and
+  expired holds are final.
+- **Balance** — what a member owes right now: posted charges minus payments.
+  Never negative, because the library keeps no credit.
+- **Blocked** — a member whose balance is at or above an action's block
+  threshold: 10.00 for checkout, 5.00 for placing a hold (ADR 0003), and any
+  amount at all for renewing (ADR 0007). A blocked member can still
+  return copies and pay.
+- **Charge** — an amount added to an account: an overdue fine, a no-show fee or
+  a manual charge.
+- **Collect** — a member checking out the copy set aside for their hold (or any
+  copy of the title), which fulfils the hold.
+- **Fine (overdue fine)** — the charge posted when a copy comes back late:
+  late days × the material's daily rate. Children are never fined. Capped
+  per loan: all fines on one loan together (including those posted at
+  renewals, ADR 0005) never exceed the title's replacement cost.
+- **Hold** — a member's place in the queue for a title whose copies are all
+  out, and the copy set aside for them when one comes back (ADR 0008).
+- **Hold shelf** — where set-aside copies wait to be collected
+  (`CopyStatus.ON_HOLD_SHELF`). Only the member they are set aside for can
+  borrow them.
+- **Late day** — a day after a loan's due date, up to and including the return
+  day, on which the library is open. Sundays are never late days.
+- **Manual charge** — a charge staff add by hand, always with a reason.
+- **No-show fee** — a 1.00 charge when a ready hold expires because the
+  member did not collect by its pickup date (ADR 0004). Counts towards blocks
+  like a fine. Children never pay it. Cancelling a hold never charges it.
+- **Payment** — an amount a member pays off their balance. Must be whole cents and
+  no more than the balance.
+- **Pickup date** (`pickup_by`) — the last day a ready hold can be collected:
+  the set-aside day + 7 calendar days, moved to the Monday if it lands on a
+  Sunday (ADR 0004). The hold expires on the first daily run after it.
+- **Pickup time** — the 7 calendar days a set-aside copy waits for the member
+  (see pickup date).
+- **Posted** — recorded in the account. A fine is posted when the copy is
+  returned or when an overdue loan is renewed, not while the loan is simply
+  still out.
+- **Queue (holds queue)** — a title's active holds in the order they were placed.
+  The first waiting hold is "first in line".
+- **Ready hold** — a hold whose copy is set aside on the hold shelf.
+- **Renewal** — extending an open loan in place (same loan, same
+  `borrowed_on`) to a new due date: the renewal day + the loan period, Sunday
+  moving to Monday. Books only, at most 2 per loan (`Loan.renewals`), from the
+  renewal window onwards (ADR 0009). Renewing an overdue loan posts the fine
+  built up so far (ADR 0005). Refused while anyone is waiting for the title
+  (ADR 0006) or while the member owes anything (ADR 0007).
+- **Renewal window** — from 5 calendar days before a loan's due date onwards,
+  with no upper end: overdue loans can still be renewed (ADR 0009).
+- **Set aside** — giving a returned, newly added or freed copy to the first
+  waiting hold on its title. The copy moves to the hold shelf and the hold
+  becomes ready.
+- **Waiting hold** — a hold in the queue with no copy set aside yet.
