+# SPEC: Renewals
+
+## Why
+
+Members ask to keep books longer. Today staff do it by returning the copy and
+checking it out again, which breaks the loan history: one borrowing becomes
+several loans, and a late return-and-recheck can hide lateness. A renewal
+extends the open loan in place, so the history keeps one loan with a count of
+how many times it was renewed. Earlier specs: `docs/specs/0001-fines.md`
+(fines and accounts), `docs/specs/0002-holds.md` (holds). Rules settled
+earlier: ADR 0005 (fine on renewal, per-loan cap), ADR 0006 (no renewal while
+anyone waits), ADR 0007 (zero balance). Rules settled for this spec: ADR 0009.
+
+## Interface (fixed by the request — other code calls exactly this)
+
+- `LendingService.renew(loan_id: str) -> Loan` in `src/lending/service.py` —
+  renews the open loan in place (same `loan_id`) and returns it.
+- `Loan` in `src/lending/models.py` gets a field `renewals: int` (default `0`):
+  how many times the loan has been renewed.
+- Add `RenewalRefused(LendingError)` to `src/lending/errors.py` for renewals
+  that can't be granted; unknown loan ids keep raising `LoanNotFound`, and keep
+  using the other existing error classes where they already fit.
+
+`checkout` and `return_copy` keep their signatures.
+
+## Rules
+
+- A renewal is **not a new loan**. The loan keeps its `loan_id`, `copy_id`,
+  `member_id` and `borrowed_on`, and the copy stays `ON_LOAN`. Only `due_on`
+  and `renewals` change (and a fine may be posted, below).
+- **New due date:** the renewal day + the normal loan period (21 days for
+  books), moved to the Monday if it lands on a Sunday, the same as a checkout.
+- **Books only.** DVDs can't be renewed.
+- **At most 2 renewals per loan.**
+- **Window:** a loan can be renewed from 5 calendar days before its `due_on`
+  onwards. Overdue loans can still be renewed.
+- **Holds (ADR 0006):** refused while any hold on the loan's title is
+  `WAITING`. Ready, fulfilled, cancelled and expired holds don't count.
+- **Balance (ADR 0007):** refused while the member owes anything (balance
+  above 0.00). This is checked before the renewal's own fine.
+- **Fine on renewal (ADR 0005):** renewing an overdue loan posts the fine built
+  up so far, worked out as if the copy were returned on the renewal day (same
+  late days, rates and child exemption). After that, lateness counts from the
+  new due date only. Every late day is charged once.
+- **Per-loan cap (ADR 0005):** all fines posted for one loan, at renewals and
+  at the return together, never exceed the title's replacement cost. This
+  changes `return_copy` too.
+- The loan limit and the 10.00 borrowing block don't apply to renewing.
+- Errors: unknown loan id → `LoanNotFound`; balance above zero →
+  `AccountBlocked`; loan already returned, DVD, limit reached, too early, or a
+  waiting hold → `RenewalRefused`. When more than one reason applies, any of
+  the matching errors is acceptable.
+- A refused renewal changes nothing: no fine, same `due_on`, same `renewals`.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+Dates use 2026: Mondays in March are 2, 9, 16, 23 and 30; Sundays are 1, 8,
+15, 22 and 29 March and 5, 12, 19 and 26 April. A book borrowed Mon 2 March is
+due Mon 23 March.
+
+Granting a renewal
+1. A new loan has `renewals == 0`.
+2. Renewing the book due Mon 23 March on Thu 19 March returns the same `Loan`
+   (same `loan_id`, `copy_id`, `member_id`, `borrowed_on` 2 March) with
+   `due_on` Thu 9 April and `renewals == 1`. `get_loan` returns the same
+   values.
+3. The renewed loan is still open. The copy stays `ON_LOAN`, and
+   `loan_history` and `open_loans` still show exactly one loan for it.
+4. A renewal whose new due date lands on a Sunday moves to the Monday: renewed
+   Sun 22 March, it is due Mon 13 April.
+5. A loan can be renewed a second time (counted from the second renewal day);
+   `renewals` becomes 2.
+6. A child member can renew a book.
+7. A member at their loan limit can still renew.
+
+Refusals
+8. A third renewal raises `RenewalRefused`.
+9. Due Mon 23 March: renewing on Wed 18 March works, and renewing on Tue
+   17 March raises `RenewalRefused`.
+10. An overdue loan can be renewed.
+11. Renewing a DVD loan raises `RenewalRefused`, even inside the window.
+12. Renewing a returned loan raises `RenewalRefused`.
+13. Renewing an unknown loan id raises `LoanNotFound`.
+14. Renewing while the member's balance is above zero raises `AccountBlocked`.
+    A balance of 0.01 is enough. After paying the balance in full, the renewal
+    works.
+15. Renewing while a hold on the title is `WAITING` raises `RenewalRefused`.
+    Once no hold on the title is waiting (for example, the hold has become
+    `READY` because another copy came back, or it was cancelled), the renewal
+    works.
+16. A refused renewal (for any reason) leaves `due_on`, `renewals`, the
+    balance and the copy status unchanged.
+
+Fines
+17. Renewing a loan that isn't overdue posts nothing.
+18. A book due Mon 23 March renewed on Tue 31 March (7 late days; Sunday 29
+    doesn't count) posts a 1.75 overdue fine with that `loan_id`. The new due
+    date is Tue 21 April.
+19. After the renewal in 18 (and paying the fine), returning on Thu 23 April
+    posts 0.50 (22 and 23 April only). No late day before the renewal is
+    charged again.
+20. A child renewing an overdue book is charged nothing.
+21. The cap is per loan: for a book with replacement cost 2.00, renewing on
+    Tue 31 March posts 1.75, and returning on Mon 27 April (5 late days,
+    1.25 calculated) posts only 0.25. The loan's total fines are 2.00.
+22. Once a loan's fines reach the cap, a later late renewal or late return
+    posts nothing.
+23. A loan never renewed is fined on return exactly as before.
+
+Regression
+24. All existing tests still pass, and `checkout` and `return_copy` keep their
+    signatures.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Self-service or online renewal; renewals happen at the desk.
+- Notices of any kind (due-date reminders, renewal confirmations).
+- A per-renewal history beyond the `renewals` count.
+- Staff overriding any refusal.
+- Automatic renewal.
+- Renewing DVDs.
+- Persistence beyond the in-memory repository.
