@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# 0002 — Member account is a ledger with no credit, and blocks at 10.00
+
+## Context
+
+Members need a balance that fines, manual staff charges and payments all act
+on, and a rule that stops people who owe too much from borrowing.
+
+## Decision
+
+- The account is an append-only ledger of entries (fine, manual charge,
+  payment). The balance is calculated from the entries and never stored.
+- Amounts are `Decimal` in whole cents and always positive. Anything else is
+  `InvalidAmount`.
+- The library keeps no credit. A payment larger than the balance is refused,
+  so the balance never goes below zero.
+- A member with a balance of 10.00 or more (`policy.BORROW_BLOCK_THRESHOLD`, renamed from `BLOCK_THRESHOLD` per ADR 0003) is
+  blocked from checkout (`AccountBlocked`). Returning and paying always work.
+- A refused checkout, charge or payment changes nothing.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Waivers and refunds, if added later, are new entry kinds. Existing entries
+  are never edited.
+- Because there is no credit, prepaying and overpaying cannot happen, so the
+  desk must take the exact balance or less.
diff --git a/docs/adr/0003-holds-blocked-at-five.md b/docs/adr/0003-holds-blocked-at-five.md
