+# 0003 — Placing a hold is blocked at a balance of 5.00
+
+Status: accepted (2026-10-28) for the holds feature, which is not built yet.
+
+## Context
+
+Holds come next after fines. A hold sets a copy aside for one member, so
+nobody else can borrow it while it waits. The owner does not want copies tied up for
+members who already owe money.
+
+## Decision
+
+- A member whose balance is 5.00 or more cannot place a hold. Exactly 5.00
+  is blocked.
+- The refusal raises `AccountBlocked`, the same error checkout uses.
+- The hold bar (5.00) is deliberately lower than the borrowing bar (10.00,
+  ADR 0002). They are separate policy values, not one shared threshold.
+- As with every refusal (ADR 0002), a refused hold changes nothing.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- `policy` needs a block threshold for each action (borrow 10.00, hold 5.00) in place of the
+  single `BLOCK_THRESHOLD`/`is_blocked` used today.
+- A member owing between 5.00 and 9.99 can still borrow from the shelf but
+  cannot place a hold.
+- The balance used is the same posted balance as for checkout (ADR 0001):
+  overdue loans still out do not count.
