+# 0004 — Uncollected holds charge a 1.00 no-show fee
+
+Status: accepted (2026-10-28). Amended 2026-10-28: the owner changed the
+pickup time from 7 open days to 7 calendar days (Sunday moves to Monday)
+before holds were built; this text is the amended rule.
+
+## Context
+
+A copy set aside for a hold is unavailable to everyone else until it is
+collected. Members who never collect waste that time.
+
+## Decision
+
+- When a copy has been set aside for a member's hold and the member does not
+  collect it within the pickup time, the member is charged a 1.00 no-show
+  fee.
+- The fee goes into the same account ledger as overdue fines (ADR 0002) and
+  counts towards both blocks (borrow 10.00, hold 5.00) like any fine.
+- Children never pay the no-show fee, the same exemption as overdue fines
+  (`policy.FINE_EXEMPT`).
+- **Pickup time is 7 calendar days** after the day the copy is set aside. The
+  last day to collect (the hold's `pickup_by`) is the set-aside day + 7 days;
+  if that is a closed day (Sunday) it moves to the next open day (Monday),
+  the same way a due date does (`policy.next_open_day`). The owner set this
+  on 2026-10-28, replacing an earlier "7 open days" rule.
+- The member can still collect on the `pickup_by` day itself. If they have not
+  collected by the end of it, the hold expires and the fee is charged.
+- A copy passed on to the next member in line after an expiry or a
+  cancellation gets a fresh pickup time counted from the day it is passed on.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The fee is a new ledger entry kind or reason, posted once per expired hold.
+  It is not counted in late days and the replacement-cost cap does not apply.
+- The fee amount and the pickup time belong in `policy`.
+- Posting the fee needs a trigger when the pickup time runs out, through the
+  injected `Clock`. The holds work chose a daily job (ADR 0008).
+- Cancelling a hold, even one already set aside, charges no fee.
