+# 0005 — Renewing an overdue loan charges the fine so far
+
+Status: accepted (2026-10-28) for the renewals feature, which comes after holds and is not built yet.
+Note (2026-10-28): DVDs turned out not to be renewable (ADR 0009). The DVD
+worked example below still shows the cap arithmetic, which applies to books
+the same way.
+
+## Context
+
+Fines are calculated from a loan's `due_on` when the copy comes back
+(ADR 0001). A renewal moves `due_on`. Without a rule, renewing an overdue loan
+would quietly wipe out the lateness before the renewal.
+
+## Decision
+
+- Renewing a loan that is already overdue charges the late fine built up so
+  far as part of the renewal.
+- That fine is calculated exactly as if the copy had been returned on the renewal day,
+  with the same open-day counting, rates and child exemption
+  (`policy.overdue_fine`).
+- After the renewal, lateness is counted against the new due date only.
+- Lateness before a renewal must never just disappear. Every late day is
+  charged once, either at a renewal or at the return.
+- **The cap is per loan.** The total of all fines posted for one loan, across
+  every renewal and the final return together, never exceeds the title's
+  replacement cost. Each new fine is limited to the cap minus what that loan
+  has already been fined. Once the cap is reached, further fines on that loan
+  are zero and nothing is posted.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- This adds a second point, the renewal, where a fine is charged. The rule
+  "posted on return, never before" in ADR 0001 then reads "posted on return
+  or on renewal". A loan that is still out and not renewed still adds nothing.
+- The renewal and its fine must happen together: a refused renewal posts no fine
+  and leaves `due_on` alone.
+- `return_copy` caps each fine on its own today, which is correct only
+  while a loan can be fined once. The renewals work must change both
+  `return_copy` and the renewal to subtract the loan's earlier fines. Fine
+  entries already carry `loan_id` for this.
+- Worked example (DVD, replacement cost 12.00): renewed 8 open days late →
+  8.00 charged. Later returned 6 open days past the new due date → 6.00
+  calculated, but only 4.00 is charged. The loan's total is 12.00.
diff --git a/docs/adr/0006-no-renewal-while-members-wait.md b/docs/adr/0006-no-renewal-while-members-wait.md
