index 0000000..d9d1266
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0006-no-renewal-while-members-wait.md
@@ -0,0 +1,30 @@
+# 0006 — Loans can't be renewed while anyone is waiting for the title
+
+Status: accepted (2026-10-28) for the renewals feature, which comes after holds
+and is not built yet.
+
+## Context
+
+Holds (ADR 0008) let members queue for a title when every copy is out. A
+renewal keeps a copy out longer. If renewals were allowed regardless, a member
+could keep a copy indefinitely while others wait in the queue.
+
+## Decision
+
+- While at least one hold on a title is **waiting** (in the queue, no copy set
+  aside yet), no loan of a copy of that title can be renewed.
+- Holds that are **ready** (a copy is already on the hold shelf for that
+  member) do not count: that member already has their copy. Neither do
+  fulfilled, cancelled or expired holds.
+- The check is per title, not per copy: holds are placed on titles, so any
+  loan of the title would satisfy the queue when it comes back.
+- As with every refusal, a refused renewal changes nothing: no fine is posted
+  and `due_on` stays the same (ADR 0005).
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The renewals work needs to ask the holds side "is anyone waiting for this
+  title?", which means active holds in `WAITING` status only.
+- Once the last waiting hold becomes ready, is cancelled or is fulfilled,
+  loans of the title can be renewed again.
+- Which error class the refusal uses is left to the renewals work.
diff --git a/docs/adr/0007-renewal-requires-zero-balance.md b/docs/adr/0007-renewal-requires-zero-balance.md
