index 0000000..e182b23
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0007-renewal-requires-zero-balance.md
@@ -0,0 +1,29 @@
+# 0007 — Renewing needs a zero balance
+
+Status: accepted (2026-10-28) for the renewals feature, which comes after holds
+and is not built yet.
+
+## Context
+
+Borrowing is blocked at 10.00 (ADR 0002) and placing a hold at 5.00 (ADR 0003).
+The owner wants renewals to be stricter still: a renewal is a convenience, and
+members who owe anything should settle up first.
+
+## Decision
+
+- A member whose balance is anything above zero when they ask to renew
+  cannot renew. They must pay the whole balance first.
+- The balance checked is the posted balance at the moment of asking (ADR 0001),
+  **before** any fine the renewal itself would post (ADR 0005). A member who owes
+  nothing can therefore renew an overdue loan, and the renewal posts its
+  fine as usual.
+- This is a third, separate block threshold (any amount owed), next to the
+  borrowing (10.00) and hold (5.00) thresholds. It is not shared with them.
+- As with every refusal, a refused renewal changes nothing.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- `policy` gains a renewal block alongside the per-action borrowing and hold blocks.
+- Children are not fined, but they can still owe manual charges, so they are
+  blocked from renewing in the same way.
+- Which error class the refusal uses is left to the renewals work.
diff --git a/docs/adr/0008-holds-queue-per-title.md b/docs/adr/0008-holds-queue-per-title.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..9d11c97
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/adr/0008-holds-queue-per-title.md
@@ -0,0 +1,47 @@
+# 0008 — Holds are a first-come queue per title, cleared by a daily job
+
+Status: accepted (2026-10-28), built with the holds feature.
+
+## Context
+
+Members want to queue for a title when every copy is out. We needed to settle
+what a hold is attached to, when a copy is set aside, how uncollected copies
+are released (ADR 0004 left the trigger open), and how holds interact with
+checkout. Later work (renewals, ADR 0006) depends on these rules.
+
+## Decision
+
+- A hold is on a **title**, never a particular copy. The holds on a title are
+  served strictly in the order they were placed. Staff cannot reorder them.
+- A hold is `WAITING` until a copy is set aside for it, then `READY` with a
+  `copy_id` and a `pickup_by` (ADR 0004). It ends `FULFILLED`, `CANCELLED` or
+  `EXPIRED`. Final states are never reopened.
+- **No copy sits on the shelf while someone waits.** Every copy that comes
+  back is offered to the queue first: a return, a newly added copy, or a copy
+  freed by an expired or cancelled ready hold. It goes to the first waiting
+  hold, or back on the shelf (`AVAILABLE`) if nobody is waiting. Because of this,
+  a hold may only be placed when no copy is `AVAILABLE`.
+- A hold may also only be placed when at least one copy is out (on loan or on
+  the hold shelf), and not by a member who already has an active hold on the
+  title or a copy of it on loan.
+- A copy set aside on the hold shelf (`CopyStatus.ON_HOLD_SHELF`) can only be
+  checked out by that hold's member. The checkout still goes through the
+  normal rules (borrowing block, loan limit). A refused collection leaves the
+  hold as it was.
+- Borrowing **any** copy of the title collects that member's ready hold, and
+  the copy that was set aside for them is offered to the queue.
+- **Trigger:** expiry is a daily job, `LendingService.expire_holds()`, run
+  through the injected `Clock`. It expires every ready hold whose `pickup_by` is
+  before today. Running it more than once on the same day, or after missed
+  days, still expires each hold once and charges one no-show fee per hold.
+- Waiting holds never expire. They stay until they are cancelled or served.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- Invariant: a title never has an `AVAILABLE` copy and a `WAITING` hold at
+  the same time.
+- Pickup time counts from the day of the action that set the copy aside. For
+  a copy passed on by the daily job, that is the day the job runs. A late job
+  therefore gives the next member their full 7 days.
+- Renewals must check the queue for `WAITING` holds only (ADR 0006).
+- No notification is built. Members find out at the desk.
