+++ b/docs/specs/0002-holds.md
@@ -0,0 +1,175 @@
+# SPEC: Holds
+
+## Why
+
+When every copy of a title is out, members can only keep asking at the desk.
+Holds let a member join a queue for the title. A returned copy is set aside for
+the first person in line, who gets a fixed time to collect it. A daily job clears
+holds nobody collected, charges the no-show fee and passes the copy on. Earlier
+specs: `docs/specs/0001-fines.md` (fines and accounts).
+
+## Interface (fixed by the request — other code calls exactly this)
+
+On `LendingService` in `src/lending/service.py`:
+
+- `place_hold(member_id: str, isbn: str) -> Hold`
+- `cancel_hold(hold_id: str) -> Hold`
+- `expire_holds() -> list[Hold]` (the daily job; returns the holds it expired)
+- `holds_for(isbn: str) -> list[Hold]` (active holds on the title, first in line first)
+- `return_copy` and `checkout` keep their signatures.
+
+In `src/lending/models.py`:
+
+- dataclass `Hold(hold_id: str, member_id: str, isbn: str, placed_on: date, status: HoldStatus, copy_id: str | None, pickup_by: date | None)`
+- enum `HoldStatus` with `WAITING, READY, FULFILLED, CANCELLED, EXPIRED`
+- new member `CopyStatus.ON_HOLD_SHELF`
+
+In `src/lending/errors.py`:
+
+- `HoldNotAllowed(LendingError)` and `HoldNotFound(LendingError)`. The existing
+  error classes are still used where they already fit.
+
+## Rules
+
+- A hold is on a **title**, not a particular copy. Holds on a title form a
+  queue in the order they were placed.
+- **Active** holds are `WAITING` (in the queue) or `READY` (a copy is set aside
+  on the hold shelf for that member). `FULFILLED`, `CANCELLED` and `EXPIRED` are
+  final.
+- **Placing a hold** is allowed only when no copy of the title is on the shelf
+  and at least one copy is out (on loan or on the hold shelf). The member must
+  not already have an active hold on the title or a copy of it on loan, and must
+  not be blocked (balance 5.00 or more, ADR 0003). There is no limit on how many
+  holds a member can have, and children can place holds.
+- **Setting aside:** a copy that comes back (returned, or freed by an expired or
+  cancelled ready hold) or is newly added goes to the first waiting hold on its
+  title. The copy becomes `ON_HOLD_SHELF` and the hold becomes `READY`. If nobody
+  is waiting, the copy goes back on the shelf (`AVAILABLE`).
+- **Pickup date** (`pickup_by`): the set-aside day + 7 calendar days. If that is
+  a Sunday it moves to the Monday. The member can still collect on the
+  `pickup_by` day itself.
+- **Collecting:** only the member a copy is set aside for can check it out, and
+  the normal checkout rules (borrowing block at 10.00, loan limit) still apply.
+  Borrowing any copy of the title collects that member's ready hold.
+- **Expiry:** the daily job expires ready holds whose `pickup_by` is before
+  today. Each expiry charges the 1.00 no-show fee (children exempt, ADR 0004)
+  and passes the copy on. Waiting holds never expire.
+- **Cancelling** a waiting or ready hold charges nothing. A cancelled ready hold
+  passes its copy on.
+- A refused operation changes nothing.
+
+## Acceptance criteria
+
+Dates use March 2026, where Mondays are 2, 9, 16, 23 and 30 and Sundays are 1,
+8, 15, 22 and 29.
+
+Placing a hold
+1. When every copy of a title is on loan, `place_hold` returns a `Hold` with a
+   new `hold_id`, the given `member_id` and `isbn`, `placed_on` = today, status
+   `WAITING`, `copy_id` None and `pickup_by` None.
+2. `place_hold` raises `HoldNotAllowed` when any copy of the title is
+   `AVAILABLE`.
+3. `place_hold` raises `HoldNotAllowed` for a title with no copies, or whose
+   copies are all `WITHDRAWN`.
+4. A hold can be placed when no copy is on the shelf and the only copies that
+   are out are on the hold shelf for other members.
+5. `place_hold` raises `HoldNotAllowed` when the member already has an active
+   (`WAITING` or `READY`) hold on the title. Once that earlier hold has been
+   cancelled, expired or fulfilled, a new hold is allowed again (if the other
+   rules allow it).
+6. `place_hold` raises `HoldNotAllowed` when the member has a copy of the title
+   on loan.
+7. `place_hold` raises `AccountBlocked` when the member's balance is 5.00 or
+   more. Exactly 5.00 blocks, and 4.99 does not.
+8. A member with a balance between 5.00 and 9.99 can still check out a copy
+   from the shelf.
+9. A child member can place a hold. A member can hold several different titles
+   at once.
+10. `place_hold` raises `MemberNotFound` for an unknown member and
+    `TitleNotFound` for an unknown ISBN.
+11. A refused `place_hold` (for any reason) creates no hold: `holds_for` is
+    unchanged, and so are copy statuses and the balance.
+
+The queue
+12. `holds_for(isbn)` returns the active holds on the title in the order they
+    were placed, first in line first. It does not include fulfilled,
+    cancelled or expired holds.
+13. `holds_for` returns an empty list for a title with no holds and raises
+    `TitleNotFound` for an unknown ISBN.
+
+Setting aside on return
+14. Returning a copy of a title with a waiting hold sets the copy aside for the
+    first person in line. The copy becomes `ON_HOLD_SHELF`, and that hold
+    becomes `READY` with `copy_id` = the returned copy and `pickup_by` set.
+    Holds further back stay `WAITING`.
+15. Returning a copy of a title with no waiting holds shelves it (`AVAILABLE`),
+    as before.
+16. `return_copy` still returns the same closed `Loan` and still posts any
+    overdue fine when it sets the copy aside.
+17. `pickup_by` is the set-aside day + 7 days: set aside on Mon 9 March, collect by
+    Mon 16 March. If that lands on a Sunday it moves to the Monday: set aside on
+    Sun 15 March, collect by Mon 23 March.
+18. Adding a new copy (`add_copy`) to a title with a waiting hold sets the new
+    copy aside for the first person in line, in the same way as a return.
+
+Collecting
+19. The member a copy is set aside for can check it out. The checkout returns a
+    normal `Loan`, the copy becomes `ON_LOAN`, and the hold becomes `FULFILLED`
+    and leaves `holds_for`.
+20. Anyone else checking out a copy on the hold shelf gets `CopyNotAvailable`.
+    The copy stays `ON_HOLD_SHELF` and the hold stays `READY`.
+21. The member can still collect on the `pickup_by` day itself.
+22. Collecting is still a checkout. If the member's balance is 10.00 or more it
+    raises `AccountBlocked`, and at their loan limit it raises
+    `LoanLimitReached`. After a refusal the hold stays `READY` with the same
+    `pickup_by`, and the copy stays `ON_HOLD_SHELF`.
+23. If a member with a ready hold checks out a different `AVAILABLE` copy of
+    the same title, that hold becomes `FULFILLED` with `copy_id` = the copy
+    they borrowed. The copy that was set aside for them goes to the next
+    waiting hold, or back on the shelf if nobody is waiting.
+24. `withdraw_copy` on a copy that is `ON_HOLD_SHELF` raises `CopyNotAvailable`.
+
+Expiry (daily job)
+25. `expire_holds` expires every `READY` hold whose `pickup_by` is before today
+    and returns those holds (status `EXPIRED`) in placement order.
+26. A hold is not expired on its `pickup_by` day. The first run on any later day
+    expires it, even if the job did not run for several days.
+27. Running `expire_holds` a second time on the same day expires nothing and
+    returns an empty list.
+28. Each expired hold charges its adult member exactly one no-show fee of 1.00.
+    A child member is charged nothing.
+29. The no-show fee counts towards both blocks: an expiry that brings the
+    balance to 5.00 blocks placing holds, and one that brings it to 10.00
+    blocks checkout.
+30. The copy of an expired hold goes to the next waiting hold on the title,
+    which becomes `READY` with `pickup_by` = the day of the run + 7 days (a
+    Sunday moves to the Monday). If nobody is waiting, the copy becomes
+    `AVAILABLE`.
+31. `expire_holds` never expires `WAITING` holds, however old they are.
+
+Cancelling
+32. `cancel_hold` on a `WAITING` hold returns it as `CANCELLED`. It leaves the
+    queue, and the holds behind it move up.
+33. `cancel_hold` on a `READY` hold returns it as `CANCELLED`, and its copy
+    goes to the next waiting hold (with `pickup_by` = today + 7 days, a Sunday
+    moving to the Monday) or back on the shelf if nobody is waiting.
+34. Cancelling never charges a fee.
+35. `cancel_hold` raises `HoldNotAllowed` on a hold that is `FULFILLED`,
+    `CANCELLED` or `EXPIRED`, and changes nothing.
+36. `cancel_hold` raises `HoldNotFound` for an unknown hold id.
+
+Regression
+37. All existing tests still pass. `checkout` and `return_copy` keep their
+    signatures.
+
+## Non-goals
+
+- Telling members that a copy is ready (notices of any kind).
+- Holds on one particular copy instead of a title.
+- Staff overriding or reordering the queue.
+- Pausing or suspending holds.
+- Expiring waiting holds after some time.
+- Limits on how many holds a member can have.
+- Renewals. Their rules about holds and balances are recorded for later in
+  ADRs 0006 and 0007.
+- Persistence beyond the in-memory repository.
